[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3852609697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3852609697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3852609697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7loiih","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T10:24:51Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T10:24:51Z","body":"I'd say the note is for overriding `SkeletonModifier3D`, not the subclasses:\n> This node should be used to implement custom IK solvers, constraints, or skeleton physics.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3852609697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853561418","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853561418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853561418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lsK5K","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T13:11:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T13:11:09Z","body":"> I'd say the note is for overriding SkeletonModifier3D, not the subclasses.\n\nProbably.\n\nWe're in a strange place where native classes like these are both:\n\n  1. Concrete implementations we use to do all the heavy lifting, and,\n  2. Cannot be used like classes defined in GDScript or other languages with virtual functions.\n  3. ...or be used like `Node`'s methods that are marked `virtual` in the docs, like `_ready` or `_input`, which can define methods anywhere in the hierarchy which will be called (but cannot call `super`)\n\nA doc fix here is probably appropriate, but I'm not sure how to word it without just saying \"virtual functions won't work if they are implemented by a native superclass.\"\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853561418/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853572758","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853572758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853572758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lsNqW","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T13:13:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T13:13:09Z","body":"It's not that they don't work it's that they aren't used, because the behavior is implemented\n\nI'm not sure how more clear we can be than what we've already had, but we could add a \"derived classes can't be extended to create custom behavior\", making the implied explicit ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853572758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853655382","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853655382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853655382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lsh1W","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T13:27:12Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T13:27:12Z","body":"That makes sense.  This probably belongs in broader GDScript documentation: the only real documentation I can find describing the `virtual` qualifier is [this warning](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/gdscript/gdscript_basics.html#classes:~:text=In%20Godot%204%2C%20even%20shadowing%20may%20not%20always%20work).\n\n> Note that this does not apply to virtual methods such as _ready(), _process() and others (marked with the virtual qualifier in the documentation and the names start with an underscore). These methods are specifically for customizing engine behavior and can be overridden in GDScript. Signals and notifications can also be useful for these purposes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853655382/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853783477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853783477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853783477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ltBG1","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T13:47:56Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T13:47:56Z","body":"I disagree, this is specific to this case, it's completely unrelated to `virtual` in general, it's based on if the class calls the virtual method at all\n\nThe method is correctly overridden, it's just never called because it's not meant to, the same way as the virtual methods for `Texture` can't be overridden in `Texture2D` to change its behavior","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853783477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853876273","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853876273","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853876273,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ltXwx","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:04:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:04:16Z","body":"Got ya, thanks.\n\nDo we have a way to mark/hint these \"non-virtual virtuals\" (from the perspective of a GDScript consumer) so `NATIVE_METHOD_OVERRIDE` can be raised in the editor?\n\nIf it's just an implementation detail (the implementor deciding not to call virtual method for performance, etc reasons), I imagine they'd have to be manually annotated for something like the above warning to work.\n\nThere was nothing I can find, so I was going to put together a proposal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853876273/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853881980","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853881980","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853881980,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ltZJ8","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:05:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:05:34Z","body":"But they aren't non-virtual, again this has *nothing* to do with them being virtual, this should just be clarified in the class, I don't think this needs any complex solution, I think you've misunderstood how virtual functions work","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853881980/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853984683","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3853984683","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3853984683,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ltyOr","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:19:22Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:19:22Z","body":">But they aren't non-virtual, again this has nothing to do with them being virtual\n\nI'm sorry, I should have said these \"effectively non-virtual\" functions, from the perspective of a GDSCript user.  Methods that can no longer be implemented in a subclass in a useful way, despite the function being marked `virtual` in the super-super class.\n\n> I think you've misunderstood how virtual functions work\n\nI think you're right.  \n\nMy understanding is from languages I've used in the past, and the few lines that exist in the Godot documentation that I linked above. Those did not dissuade me from my previous understanding.\n\nI was not aware we have \"still technically virtual but an intervening class implementation can choose not to call it\" virtual methods, which is where I think my misunderstanding came from.  It felt like a bug.\n\nThis is the case I think would be nice if the editor could warn about, if given metadata inside the implementation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3853984683/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854023153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854023153","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854023153,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lt7nx","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:25:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:25:05Z","body":"I don't think this needs complex engine code to deal with incorrect use, I don't think most people are confused about this and if we make the documentation more explicit people are unlikely to be confused at all\n\nNote that the documentation already does state that *that* node, i.e. `SkeletonModifier3D`, should be used to create custom behavior, we can make this more explicit by saying \"extend this class and override ...\" and that should be enough","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854023153/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854158543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854158543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854158543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lucrP","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:50:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:50:17Z","body":"> I don't think this needs complex engine code to deal\n\nI haven't proposed any complex engine code.  Method metadata (`MethodInfo`/`MethodFlags`) exists now.\n\n> I don't think most people are confused about this and if we make the documentation more explicit people are unlikely to be confused at all\n\n[Here](https://www.reddit.com/r/godot/comments/1pnlymo/46_ik_nodes_dont_have_process_modification/) is someone else running into this exact issue last month (and coincidentally, the exact case I hit this morning.)\n\n> Note that the documentation already does state that that node, i.e. SkeletonModifier3D\n\nIf Godot's meaning of `virtual` is this out of the norm (it can be optional from a GDScript perspective), I think it should be decently documented.  \n\nI'd argue the common understanding of `virtual` is that a method is `virtual` and can be overridden, or not virtual and cannot be overridden, not a secret third thing that doesn't inherit.\n\nI think I've veered this Issue too far off course of my original report.  If this is expected behavior, and an editor warning is super-complicated, I'd be happy with a doc fix from someone who can word it without my misunderstanding of virtual functions.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854158543/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854179693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854179693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854179693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7luh1t","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T14:54:27Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T14:56:42Z","body":"I think you've gotten stuck on `virtual`, this has again nothing to do with that, the method is overridden\n\nThere isn't anything optional about that here, please go back through my explanation, you are focusing on the wrong thing here, there's nothing that's odd or unusual about the virtual nature of the method, it's just never called because it's not used when the behavior is implemented elsewhere\n\nSo let's focus on the documentation clarifying that it's just `SkeletonModifier3D` that *uses* the virtual method because it *doesn't* implement any behavior like that itself, but other derived classes do\n\nAdding a whole system to error or warn when a method is overridden in a different context would be a lot of work, for an exceptionally unusual misunderstanding, unless there are more than two cases you can find, and again that'd be trivially solved by documenting this specific thing in this specific class\n\nFor example `_property_get_revert` isn't called unless `_property_can_revert` is overridden and returns `true`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854179693/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854348695","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854348695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854348695,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lvLGX","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T15:20:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T15:22:05Z","body":"Awesome.  I'm happy to work on a doc PR:\n\n  - SkeletonModifier3D uses the `_process_modification{,_with_delta}` to allow subclasses to implement their behavior.  This is already documented great.\n  - Native subclasses of SkeletonModifier3D (do not/may not?) call overridden `_process_modification_with_delta` on subclasses: using the signal is the only supported way to hook into this.\n  - GDScript **direct** subclasses of SkeletonModifier3D allow for their subclasses to also override parent GDScript implementations of `_process_modification_with_delta`, use `super`, etc.\n\nI believe this describes the current behavior.  Is there anything I'm missing?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854348695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854367738","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854367738","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854367738,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lvPv6","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T15:24:20Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T15:24:20Z","body":"Doesn't need to be that big a change, just specify that users should extend `SkeletonModifier3D` to create custom behavior","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854367738/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854390744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115886#issuecomment-3854390744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115886","id":3854390744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7lvVXY","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-05T15:28:39Z","updated_at":"2026-02-05T15:28:39Z","body":"Thanks.  In that case, I believe this is already sufficiently documented.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3854390744/reactions